&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Thatch&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For most people, health insurance is something that happens to them: a plan chosen by someone else, with little room to fit their life. Thatch is changing that. We help companies give every employee a real healthcare budget instead of a one-size-fits-all plan, so people can choose the coverage and care that works for them, and employers get predictable costs they can control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s a simple idea, but making it real means solving hard problems across healthcare, payments, and technology, and we’re just getting started. We look for people who like solving complex problems, use good judgment, and are comfortable working through ambiguity. People here care deeply about our customers, take real responsibility for what gets built, and are driven by doing work that matters.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mt-4&quot;&gt;As our customer base grows, so does the complexity of supporting employers, brokers, and members through the moments that matter most in their Thatch journey. The Field Account Manager (FAM) is a critical part of how we deliver on that promise — bringing high-quality, in-person support to customers and enabling proactive, ongoing education and enablement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rather than owning a named book of business, Field Account Managers operate within an account team model, partnering closely with Account Managers and Implementation Managers to enable customers and add value more widely. In practice, that might mean leading an onsite open enrollment meeting for a mid-market employer one week, hosting a webinar series the next, and helping prepare renewal materials and customer insights in between.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role blends relationship building, customer education, operational execution, and cross-functional advocacy – and it&#39;s well-suited for someone who thrives in front of customers, moves comfortably between priorities, and wants to help shape how a high-growth company scales its customer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-4 list-disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an extension of the Account Management and Implementation teams by delivering onsite support, employee education, and enrollment assistance for customers across a designated region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead employer-facing programs including open enrollment sessions, Thatch platform training, product webinars, office hours, and other engagement initiatives focused on renewals, product roadmap, and other relevant topics such as compliance and Thatch Marketplace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Account Managers to deepen customer relationships by gathering insights, identifying opportunities and risks, supporting business reviews, and helping execute strategic account plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and execute customer onsite events end-to-end, including travel logistics, stakeholder alignment, presentation delivery, and post-event follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a customer advocate by surfacing feedback, identifying recurring themes, and partnering cross-functionally with Product, Operations, and Support to drive improvements to the customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;Background we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-4 list-disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in benefits consulting, customer success, support or a related customer-facing role; an active broker license and fluency in plan advising is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and presentation skills, with the ability to build trust and engage audiences ranging from frontline employees to HR leaders and executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills and attention to detail, with experience managing multiple priorities and customer engagements simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to navigate ambiguity, solve problems independently, and operate effectively in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel regularly within a designated region to support customer meetings, open enrollment events, and company initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort analyzing customer data, preparing reporting, and translating insights into actionable recommendations that improve customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Experience we&#39;d be particularly excited about&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bilingual in Spanish and English strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Travel Expectations&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-4 mt-4 list-disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;50%+ travel during annual open enrollment season (Q4)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;What to expect&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mt-4&quot;&gt;We interview rigorously based on integrity, talent, and drive; the trust we display in our teammates from day 1 is a reflection of the confidence we have in this process. We aim to evaluate the things you’ll be doing every day as best we can, and we move quickly. Here&#39;s what to expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-8 mt-4 list-disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 minute video meeting to talk through your background and interest in Thatch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 minute video meeting with the hiring manager to dive deeper into your experience and the role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 minute video meeting to meet 2-3 members of the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 minute video meeting with the department leadership and one of our founders to discuss your approach to culture and our operating principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Estimated Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$85,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$100,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Thatch&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For most people, health insurance is something that happens to them: a plan chosen by someone else, with little room to fit their life. Thatch is changing that. We help companies give every employee a real healthcare budget instead of a one-size-fits-all plan, so people can choose the coverage and care that works for them, and employers get predictable costs they can control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s a simple idea, but making it real means solving hard problems across healthcare, payments, and technology, and we’re just getting started. We look for people who like solving complex problems, use good judgment, and are comfortable working through ambiguity. People here care deeply about our customers, take real responsibility for what gets built, and are driven by doing work that matters.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mt-4&quot;&gt;This role leads GTM Analytics within the Revenue Strategy function and reports directly to the Head of Revenue Strategy &amp;amp; Operations. You will own how Thatch measures GTM performance, understands channel economics, and governs the data foundation behind commercial decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role covers three areas: &lt;strong&gt;GTM performance and channel economics, GTM data strategy and governance, and analytical support for forecasting, planning, and executive reporting.&lt;/strong&gt; Your work is the analytical engine behind all three.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You set the analytical agenda for your areas. You decide which questions matter most, focus effort on the highest-value work, and turn findings into recommendations that change where Thatch invests. You will partner closely with Marketing, Data Science, Finance, and RevOps.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GTM Performance and Channel Economics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build performance frameworks that show GTM health across the full customer lifecycle, from lead through close, onboarding, retention, and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the framework for comparing Thatch&#39;s GTM motions: win rates, CAC, payback, and conversion by segment, geography, and channel, plus broker attribution and quoting performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Marketing on funnel and attribution, with Data Science on modeling and segmentation, and with Finance on unit economics and scenario analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot emerging trends early and recommend where to invest and where to pull back, including clear tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize the analytics roadmap by business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GTM Data Strategy and Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the GTM data strategy and set priorities for the integrity, scalability, and evolution of the GTM team’s data foundation, in partnership with Data Science.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and govern core GTM metrics, business logic, and data standards so every standing number is consistent, auditable, and reconciles with Finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set governance for definitions, lineage, quality, and usage in partnership with RevOps, Data Science, Engineering, and Finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define GTM business requirements before technical work begins. RevOps and Engineering keep ownership of technical build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize GTM data initiatives and make sequencing recommendations based on dependencies and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure data assets support critical use cases, including forecasting, pipeline management, planning, compensation, and performance measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption of governed metrics and BI across GTM teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forecasting, Planning, and Reporting Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the analytical inputs behind the forecast: pipeline snapshots, coverage, stage conversion, and pacing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supply the data and models that feed target setting, capacity planning, and compensation analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver complete, accurate analytics for board, QBR, and MBR materials on every cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flag when the data signals risk to the forecast or plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Decision Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Break down ambiguous GTM questions, combining data, financial implications, and operational context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead high-stakes segment, channel, and territory analyses from problem definition through recommendation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present findings, risks, and tradeoffs clearly to senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;Background we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-4 list-disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience.&lt;/strong&gt; 5 to 8 years in GTM analytics, RevOps, BizOps, strategy, or FP&amp;amp;A at a high-growth B2B company, with direct partnership with sales, marketing, and finance leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical depth.&lt;/strong&gt; Expert SQL. Deep experience with sales and product telemetry data, mainstream business intelligence tools.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data governance.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience owning metric definitions and data standards, and turning business requirements into technical specs in a modern data stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems thinking.&lt;/strong&gt; You understand dependencies across CRM, warehouse, BI, and GTM execution, and how a field change flows through to a board metric.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial judgment.&lt;/strong&gt; Command of GTM and SaaS metrics, including win rates, conversion, attribution, CAC, payback, and retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional influence.&lt;/strong&gt; You align Marketing, Data Science, Finance, and RevOps on shared definitions and priorities without formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive communication.&lt;/strong&gt; You deliver answers, not dashboards, and turn complex analysis into clear recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership.&lt;/strong&gt; You own the numbers, catch errors first, and raise risks early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;Experience we’d be particularly excited about&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-4 mt-4 list-disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment, balancing speed and rigor with limited resources and evolving data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;What to expect&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mt-4&quot;&gt;We interview rigorously based on integrity, talent, and drive; the trust we display in our teammates from day 1 is a reflection of the confidence we have in this process. We aim to evaluate the things you’ll be doing every day as best we can, and we move quickly. Here&#39;s what to expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-8 mt-4 list-disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 minute video meeting to talk through your background and interest in Thatch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 minute video meeting with the hiring manager to dive deeper into your experience and the role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 minute video meeting to meet 2-3 members of the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 minute video meeting with the hiring manager to work through a live case study&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 minute video meeting with department leadership to discuss alignment to our company values and career goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 minute video meeting with our founders to discuss your approach to culture and our operating principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Estimated Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$112,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$145,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Thatch&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For most people, health insurance is something that happens to them: a plan chosen by someone else, with little room to fit their life. Thatch is changing that. We help companies give every employee a real healthcare budget instead of a one-size-fits-all plan, so people can choose the coverage and care that works for them, and employers get predictable costs they can control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s a simple idea, but making it real means solving hard problems across healthcare, payments, and technology, and we’re just getting started. We look for people who like solving complex problems, use good judgment, and are comfortable working through ambiguity. People here care deeply about our customers, take real responsibility for what gets built, and are driven by doing work that matters.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;225&quot; data-end=&quot;242&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thatch is changing healthcare benefits. We give companies a way to offer every employee a health budget so they can choose the plan that fits their life, while giving employers predictable costs they can control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Healthcare is one of the biggest conversations in the country, and Thatch has a story worth telling. As Head of Communications, you’ll own how we tell it across press, thought leadership, and social. You’ll set the strategy and do the work: pitching, writing, posting, and finding the moments where Thatch should be part of the conversation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;1068&quot; data-end=&quot;1087&quot;&gt;What you will do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;1089&quot; data-end=&quot;1722&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Thatch’s communications strategy across earned media, thought leadership, and organic social.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with top reporters and land coverage that matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn company news, industry trends, and cultural moments into stories people want to talk about.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build distinct voices for Thatch and our executives across press, podcasts, and social.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn our data and expertise into original stories, reports, and points of view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow Thatch beyond a B2B benefits brand, making healthcare easier to understand and more relevant to consumers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;1729&quot; data-end=&quot;1755&quot;&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;1757&quot; data-end=&quot;2230&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in communications, ideally in healthcare, benefits, or HR tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of landing meaningful earned media and building relationships with top reporters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional writing and editorial judgment, especially around complex topics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep enough industry fluency to know what’s newsworthy and where Thatch can add to the conversation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on operating style. You’re as comfortable writing the pitch as setting the strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;2541&quot; data-end=&quot;2570&quot;&gt;Experience that stands out&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;2572&quot; data-end=&quot;2829&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built a communications function or company narrative from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turned data or industry trends into stories that earned attention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built a recognizable voice for a company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;2836&quot; data-end=&quot;2850&quot;&gt;How we work&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;2852&quot; data-end=&quot;3055&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2852&quot; data-end=&quot;2904&quot;&gt;We give people ownership and expect good judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2905&quot; data-end=&quot;2952&quot;&gt;We move quickly without compromising quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2953&quot; data-end=&quot;3003&quot;&gt;We work across functions to solve hard problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3004&quot; data-end=&quot;3055&quot;&gt;We learn from customers and continuously improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;3062&quot; data-end=&quot;3079&quot;&gt;What to expect&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3081&quot; data-end=&quot;3208&quot;&gt;We aim to keep the process thoughtful, rigorous, and efficient. Most candidates complete it within three weeks. You can expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;3210&quot; data-end=&quot;3484&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3210&quot; data-end=&quot;3253&quot;&gt;An initial conversation with a recruiter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3254&quot; data-end=&quot;3295&quot;&gt;A conversation with the hiring manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3296&quot; data-end=&quot;3366&quot;&gt;A practical exercise related to the work you&#39;ll be doing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3367&quot; data-end=&quot;3435&quot;&gt;Conversations with future teammates and cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3436&quot; data-end=&quot;3484&quot;&gt;A final conversation with our Leadership team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Estimated Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$160,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$210,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Thatch&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For most people, health insurance is something that happens to them: a plan chosen by someone else, with little room to fit their life. Thatch is changing that. We help companies give every employee a real healthcare budget instead of a one-size-fits-all plan, so people can choose the coverage and care that works for them, and employers get predictable costs they can control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s a simple idea, but making it real means solving hard problems across healthcare, payments, and technology, and we’re just getting started. We look for people who like solving complex problems, use good judgment, and are comfortable working through ambiguity. People here care deeply about our customers, take real responsibility for what gets built, and are driven by doing work that matters.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;467&quot; data-end=&quot;716&quot;&gt;Healthcare in America is notoriously complex, opaque, and outdated. We’ve been conditioned to have low expectations for the user experience in healthcare, accepting clunky portals, confusing workflows, and endless toil as the cost of doing business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;718&quot; data-end=&quot;984&quot;&gt;At Thatch, we believe great design is a missing catalyst for fixing healthcare. We’re rebuilding health benefits from the ground up to create a personalized, transparent, and genuinely joyful experience for every employee, employer, broker, and partner we work with.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;986&quot; data-end=&quot;1291&quot;&gt;As our Head of Design, you’ll lead product and brand design at Thatch and help us set a new bar for what healthcare can look and feel like. You’ll lead and grow an exceptional design team, set the creative direction for the company, and bring consumer-grade craft and polish to every experience we create.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-4 list-disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1w4gz7u&quot; data-start=&quot;1313&quot; data-end=&quot;1411&quot;&gt;Set and execute a design strategy across our product, website, brand, and marketing experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1v6ectj&quot; data-start=&quot;1412&quot; data-end=&quot;1492&quot;&gt;Lead, develop, and grow a high-performing team of product and brand designers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;8ekrkj&quot; data-start=&quot;1493&quot; data-end=&quot;1606&quot;&gt;Set a high bar for craft and create a culture of thoughtful, direct design critique and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1vzfy5a&quot; data-start=&quot;1607&quot; data-end=&quot;1721&quot;&gt;Think from first principles about complex healthcare experiences and make them simple, intuitive, and beautiful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1d80qra&quot; data-start=&quot;1722&quot; data-end=&quot;1858&quot;&gt;Partner closely with Product, Engineering, Marketing, Sales, and Operations to understand our users and ship high-impact work quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;Background we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-4 list-disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1l6jkso&quot; data-start=&quot;1888&quot; data-end=&quot;1976&quot;&gt;7+ years of design experience, including 3+ years leading and developing design teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;nsa9lh&quot; data-start=&quot;1977&quot; data-end=&quot;2070&quot;&gt;Exceptional design taste and a track record of delivering high-quality product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;olibtt&quot; data-start=&quot;2071&quot; data-end=&quot;2148&quot;&gt;Significant experience as both an individual contributor and design leader.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;yayhnf&quot; data-start=&quot;2149&quot; data-end=&quot;2245&quot;&gt;Experience setting design direction and raising the quality bar across a team or organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1i1lxl1&quot; data-start=&quot;2246&quot; data-end=&quot;2318&quot;&gt;Experience operating in a fast-moving, high-growth technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;Experience we’d be particularly excited about&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-4 mt-4 list-disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1e4nz9b&quot; data-start=&quot;2369&quot; data-end=&quot;2419&quot;&gt;Experience across both product and brand design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;i4chml&quot; data-start=&quot;2420&quot; data-end=&quot;2475&quot;&gt;Experience simplifying complex or regulated products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;xcr6f1&quot; data-start=&quot;2476&quot; data-end=&quot;2529&quot;&gt;A background spanning both B2B and B2C experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;10tg1jd&quot; data-start=&quot;2530&quot; data-end=&quot;2597&quot;&gt;Experience working in a fast-moving agency or studio environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;fcqi6u&quot; data-start=&quot;2598&quot; data-end=&quot;2651&quot;&gt;Healthcare experience is helpful, but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;What to expect&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We aim to keep the process thoughtful, rigorous, and efficient. Most candidates complete it within three weeks. You can expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;286&quot; data-end=&quot;393&quot;&gt;Recruiter Conversation: 30 minutes to discuss your background, what you’re looking for, and the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;394&quot; data-end=&quot;523&quot;&gt;Hiring Manager Conversation: 30 minutes with our President to talk about your experience and approach to design leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;524&quot; data-end=&quot;628&quot;&gt;Portfolio Review: 60 minutes with members of the design team to walk through your work and impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;629&quot; data-end=&quot;764&quot;&gt;Functional Interviews: Three 30-minute conversations with team members to go deeper into how you think, lead, and work with others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;765&quot; data-end=&quot;873&quot;&gt;Executive Conversation: 30 minutes with our CEO to discuss leadership, values, and building at Thatch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Estimated Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$220,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$290,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Thatch&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For most people, health insurance is something that happens to them: a plan chosen by someone else, with little room to fit their life. Thatch is changing that. We help companies give every employee a real healthcare budget instead of a one-size-fits-all plan, so people can choose the coverage and care that works for them, and employers get predictable costs they can control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s a simple idea, but making it real means solving hard problems across healthcare, payments, and technology, and we’re just getting started. We look for people who like solving complex problems, use good judgment, and are comfortable working through ambiguity. People here care deeply about our customers, take real responsibility for what gets built, and are driven by doing work that matters.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mt-4&quot;&gt;At Thatch, technology is how our teams get their work done, securely and without friction. As our IT Ops/Systems Engineer, you&#39;ll own the systems and access infrastructure that keeps the company running: endpoint compliance, identity and access management, and the operational backbone behind our security initiatives. This role goes beyond day-to-day support. You&#39;ll be the owner of company-wide compliance, conditional access and privileged access workflows in a Mac-first environment, with the autonomy to build the systems and automation that let us scale securely. If you want real ownership over how a fast-growing technology company manages access and identity, this role is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-4 list-disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own our technology stack including Okta, Iru, Mac, iOS, Android, Rippling MDM/SSO, 1Password, Google Workspace, Microsoft Office, Slack, Zoom, Linear, and Notion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive endpoint fleet compliance to 100% coverage across MDM, EDR, and DLP, and own remediation when devices fall out of compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer conditional access policies (device trust, managed browser enforcement) and own the exception and escalation process when legitimate access gets blocked&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Privileged Access Management (PAM) workflow, including replacing manual quarterly access reviews with automated request, approval, and time-bound removal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run trusted device and MFA enrollment, and lead remediation campaigns for weak or breached passwords&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the complete employee lifecycle experience from onboarding through offboarding, managing access control, hardware provisioning, and audit-ready documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vet and administer new SaaS tooling for SSO/IdP compliance as part of vendor onboarding, expose and remediate shadow IT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a knowledge base that empowers employees to solve common issues independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and build automation for repetitive IT and access-management tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Head of IT and Security to support company-wide initiatives and maintain our security posture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;Background we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-4 list-disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-6 years of hands-on IT support or systems engineering experience in a corporate environment, ideally including some ownership of identity/access infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certification in Network+, Security+, JAMF, Bettercloud, Okta, or comparable credentials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of SSO, 2FA, passkeys, conditional access, and password management systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience administering or implementing a PAM tool, or a clear grasp of the concepts and willingness to build one from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of security principles and best practices with proven ability to implement them at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent follow-through and organizational skills. You never let tasks fall through the cracks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;Experience we’d be particularly excited about&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-4 mt-4 list-disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving a fleet from partial to full MDM/EDR/DLP compliance, and building the exception workflow that kept support ticket volume manageable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated individuals who can work independently with minimal supervision and take ownership of projects from start to finish&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quick learners who can master new technologies with minimal guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Patient communicators with flexible, inclusive interpersonal skills who genuinely enjoy helping others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-solvers who are resilient in learning from mistakes and view technical challenges as opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;People who thrive in fast-paced environments and can adapt quickly to changing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;What to expect&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mt-4&quot;&gt;We interview rigorously based on integrity, talent, and drive; the trust we display in our teammates from day 1 is a reflection of the confidence we have in this process. We aim to evaluate the things you’ll be doing every day as best we can, and we move quickly. Here&#39;s what to expect:&lt;/p&gt;
