&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Thatch&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For most people, health insurance is something that happens to them: a plan chosen by someone else, with little room to fit their life. Thatch is changing that. We help companies give every employee a real healthcare budget instead of a one-size-fits-all plan, so people can choose the coverage and care that works for them, and employers get predictable costs they can control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s a simple idea, but making it real means solving hard problems across healthcare, payments, and technology, and we’re just getting started. We look for people who like solving complex problems, use good judgment, and are comfortable working through ambiguity. People here care deeply about our customers, take real responsibility for what gets built, and are driven by doing work that matters.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Thatch is reimagining how health benefits work. We help employers give their employees a healthcare budget to choose the coverage that works best for them, while making benefits easier to manage and costs more predictable for businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Partner Engineer to own the reliability and success of our payroll and HRIS integrations as we scale. You&#39;ll work directly with customers, integration partners, and internal teams to solve complex technical challenges, validate new integrations, and keep critical connections running reliably.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact role with real ownership from day one. You&#39;ll play a key part in delivering a seamless experience for our customers while helping our engineering team stay focused on building what&#39;s next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own integration health.&lt;/strong&gt; Monitor, troubleshoot, and resolve payroll and HRIS connection issues, ensuring integrations work reliably for our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead technical validation.&lt;/strong&gt; Partner directly with enterprise customers to test payroll integrations, identify potential issues, and ensure successful launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the technical expert.&lt;/strong&gt; Help customers and internal teams navigate complex payroll configurations, integration capabilities, and API limitations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive issues to resolution.&lt;/strong&gt; Work across customers, external partners, and engineering to diagnose problems, remove blockers, and own outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build scalable processes.&lt;/strong&gt; Develop runbooks, monitoring practices, and workflows that improve reliability and reduce recurring issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape how we scale.&lt;/strong&gt; Identify patterns and opportunities to improve our integrations, customer experience, and engineering efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in partner engineering, solutions engineering, technical integrations, or a similar customer-facing technical role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of APIs, including the ability to read documentation, troubleshoot failures, and diagnose integration issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning complex technical problems across multiple systems, stakeholders, or external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence working directly with customers, translating technical complexity into clear guidance and solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership mindset, with the ability to independently prioritize issues and drive them through resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building repeatable processes, documentation, or monitoring practices to improve operational reliability.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Experience that stands out&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payroll, HRIS, or benefits platforms, particularly complex enterprise configurations and integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with third-party APIs and integration partners, such as Finch, Merge, or similar platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building internal tools, scripts, or automations to improve integration reliability and reduce manual work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a forward-deployed engineering or technical solutions role, solving complex customer problems and translating them into scalable technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What to expect&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We aim to move quickly, and most candidates complete the process within 2–3 weeks. You can expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An initial conversation with a recruiter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A conversation with the hiring manager to discuss your experience and approach to technical problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A practical technical exercise and conversations with cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A final conversation with company leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Estimated Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$160,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$195,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Thatch&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For most people, health insurance is something that happens to them: a plan chosen by someone else, with little room to fit their life. Thatch is changing that. We help companies give every employee a real healthcare budget instead of a one-size-fits-all plan, so people can choose the coverage and care that works for them, and employers get predictable costs they can control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s a simple idea, but making it real means solving hard problems across healthcare, payments, and technology, and we’re just getting started. We look for people who like solving complex problems, use good judgment, and are comfortable working through ambiguity. People here care deeply about our customers, take real responsibility for what gets built, and are driven by doing work that matters.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mt-4&quot;&gt;At Thatch, design is one of the defining traits that sets us apart. The healthcare experience in America has long been subpar, and the bar for quality design is low — we’re raising that bar, and with it, the entire health insurance industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;412&quot; data-end=&quot;913&quot;&gt;As a designer at Thatch, you’ll craft beautiful experiences for the people using our product every day: businesses, their teams, and brokers. You’ll shape all aspects of design, including UI components for our design system, new products involving complex user interactions, and the overall strategy and vision of the design team. Your work will help create a better insurance experience that &lt;strong data-start=&quot;805&quot; data-end=&quot;910&quot;&gt;enables members to get the healthcare benefits they need while feeling calm, fulfilled, and liberated&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;915&quot; data-end=&quot;1202&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who can meet users where they are in their journey and inspire trust by delivering simple, beautiful, and well-crafted end-to-end experiences. You should be comfortable owning the entire design process, from UX strategy to product design and company branding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-4 list-disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in and shape every part of the product development process, from idea inception to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with engineering, growth, product, sales, operations, and leadership to create incredible user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain the design system and brand assets we’ll use across the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write design documentation and guidelines for internal audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Iterate on and improve our design standards, tooling, and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;Background we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-4 list-disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in product design roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Obsession with understanding and serving users and, ultimately, making their lives better&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated first principle thinking and mastery of fundamental design principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in ambiguous environments solving complex user problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance blue sky creativity and dedication to craft with bias to action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-10&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mb-4 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-3xl md:text-2xl&quot;&gt;Experience we’d be particularly excited about&lt;/h3&gt;
